{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_234cd870d6aac9a32aa5fda069a89c61d690432fcd2d258115840bf8f9d0bad7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product runs on macOS 13+ or Linux x64 and requires git 2.20+ on PATH; supported agent harnesses are Claude Code, Codex, Pi, and OpenCode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_270c260c280bd20f06162d692613176d1a8e56665778f643c12b5e6a57eb9c75"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ouijit shadows agent binaries on PATH to inject lifecycle hooks and a CLI reference into each session, letting agents create tasks, advance the board, and open panels without setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5bab2cc5a333c8b903f90830f338ddf4120029d06ab19c3b5146b7f43dd22a08"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tasks live on a kanban board; moving a card between To Do, In Progress, In Review, and Done fires a matching lifecycle hook, and starting a task creates an isolated git worktree."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5f894fe31fd20819adc5d4991dd48df00cd55b4ec4294797c35a2963756ceaff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Terminals are cards in a stack with attachable panel tabs: a script runner, a web preview, and markdown files with Mermaid diagrams; non-task shells get their own board strip."},{"claim_ids":["clm_64406e474e733694ef6b6da5a3d40c5f6edd12499e028256183f06f94f8727b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An experimental GitHub surface provides a pull request inbox, locally staged review comments, and merging, driven by the `gh` CLI with `gh auth login` as the only setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_71f73c843a2d483520389ce9d9367ae6786f45fe35cd7726c45c01135a4956f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ouijit is a task and terminal manager for running coding agents in parallel, where each task gets its own git worktree and terminal, with lifecycle hooks launching the agent CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b8457e7f488730e822425c84f102b052d97ab59acf8fe44ee96d9dc63e7d25e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each task terminal shows a diff of its worktree against a merge target, uncommitted changes, or a chosen base, with word-level highlighting and per-line notes routed to the agent in that worktree."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8a85cf2bcf2aadd90fbe7a07e04d205da3e44c728452a2d3cdba0e5086a94932"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is free and open source under AGPL-3.0, with no account, sign-in, or telemetry, and distributes self-contained builds for macOS (Apple Silicon/Intel) and Linux x64."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2ffbd6fb77fddc94805bfe8e48e5e01bdb12b837d5cefc5686ed4a93d1120c9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Quitting saves the session, and the next launch offers to restore its terminals in their worktrees, panels included; all data is stored locally in SQLite."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a898bebb64a0aad82979737d442811239b0cda75bffbb7a81493f1732d499b12"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Any terminal can run sandboxed: in a Lima VM mounting only the task's worktree, in place under Seatbelt/Landlock via nono (experimental), or under a user-supplied launcher (experimental)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_234cd870d6aac9a32aa5fda069a89c61d690432fcd2d258115840bf8f9d0bad7","clm_270c260c280bd20f06162d692613176d1a8e56665778f643c12b5e6a57eb9c75","clm_5bab2cc5a333c8b903f90830f338ddf4120029d06ab19c3b5146b7f43dd22a08","clm_5f894fe31fd20819adc5d4991dd48df00cd55b4ec4294797c35a2963756ceaff","clm_64406e474e733694ef6b6da5a3d40c5f6edd12499e028256183f06f94f8727b6","clm_71f73c843a2d483520389ce9d9367ae6786f45fe35cd7726c45c01135a4956f0","clm_7b8457e7f488730e822425c84f102b052d97ab59acf8fe44ee96d9dc63e7d25e","clm_8a85cf2bcf2aadd90fbe7a07e04d205da3e44c728452a2d3cdba0e5086a94932","clm_a2ffbd6fb77fddc94805bfe8e48e5e01bdb12b837d5cefc5686ed4a93d1120c9","clm_a898bebb64a0aad82979737d442811239b0cda75bffbb7a81493f1732d499b12"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","id":"pg_218a5388ade354e798b002b64210412c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ouijit-ouijit-readme-md-b868ef792dc7-02b64210412c.md","record_type":"page","revie